.TH "XmCreateExt18List" "library call"
.SH "NAME"
\fBXmCreateExt18List\fP,
\fBXmCreateExtended18List\fP \(em Obsolete MultiList widget creation functions
.iX "XmCreateExt18List"
.iX "creation functions" "XmCreateExt18List"
.iX "creation functions" "XmCreateExtended18List"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/Ext18List\&.h>
\fBWidget \fBXmCreateExt18List\fP\fR(
\fBWidget \fBparent\fR\fR,
\fBString \fBname\fR\fR,
\fBArgList \fBarglist\fR\fR,
\fBCardinal \fBargcount\fR\fR);
.PP
\fBWidget \fBXmCreateExtended18List\fP\fR(
\fBWidget \fBparent\fR\fR,
\fBString \fBname\fR\fR,
\fBArgList \fBarglist\fR\fR,
\fBCardinal \fBargcount\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBXmCreateExt18List\fP and \fBXmCreateExtended18List\fP create an
instance of a MultiList widget, which used to be called Ext18List, and
return the associated widget ID\&.
They are the old names of \fBXmCreateMultiList\fP, which
\fB<Xm/Ext18List\&.h>\fP declares deprecated\&.
.IP "\fIparent\fP" 10
Specifies the parent widget ID
.IP "\fIname\fP" 10
Specifies the name of the created widget
.IP "\fIarglist\fP" 10
Specifies the argument list
.IP "\fIargcount\fP" 10
Specifies the number of attribute/value pairs in the argument list
(\fIarglist\fP)
.PP
For a complete definition of MultiList and its associated resources, see
\fBXmMultiList\fP(3)\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
Returns the MultiList widget ID\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fBXmCreateMultiList\fP(3), \fBXmMultiList\fP(3) and \fBXmExt18List\fP(3)\&.
